IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-authorization.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, sections 83.031 to 83.0392: the authorization regime under which the
-- Public Safety Minister may authorize activities otherwise prohibited by subsection 83.03(2). Layer 1, written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- WHO THE REGIME IS ABOUT. Almost every provision here addresses a Minister. It is encoded for what it means to the person who applies for, holds or is
-- covered by an authorization: who is eligible, which purposes and activities are in, what the Minister may and may not do to the application and the
-- authorization, what the person must provide, and the periods that bind them. There is no seat for an official (the brief).
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29 and the ruling of 2026-11-12): JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`.
-- A function named for a power ("may") answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, when an "if" gate fails (tag GATE-A); where the text closes the gate itself
-- ("only if", "must not", "is not permitted") it answers JUST FALSE. Three groups are NOT decided here and are listed in NOTES.md for a lawyer: "may" functions
-- gated by "where", "when", "upon", "on application" or a stated period (tag GATE-B: answered JUST FALSE as the 2026-11-05 rulings say), and functions named
-- for being "eligible" (tag ENTITLED). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Periods are dates: `Date day month year`; a period in days is added with `PLUS`, in months and years with `add months` (daydate).

§ `Section 83.031 -- Definition of Public Safety Minister; designation`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.031(1) Public Safety Minister | s 83.031(1); s 83.031(1) "Public Safety Minister"
-- src:1304 | Definition of Public Safety Minister
-- src:1305 | 83.031 (1) In sections 83.032 to 83.0392, Public Safety Minister means the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness.
@ref s 83.031(1) (src:1304-1305)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.031(1) Public Safety Minister` MEANS
    IF provision's `section` AT LEAST 83.032 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 83.0392
    THEN IF `the person is the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Public Safety Minister means the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In sections 83.032 to 83.0392, Public Safety Minister means"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.031(2) the Minister may designate a person to exercise a power, or perform a duty or function | s 83.031(2)
-- src:1306 | Designation
-- src:1307 | (2) Any Minister referred to in any of sections 83.032 to 83.0392 may designate a person to exercise a power, or perform a duty or function, conferred on that Minister under those sections.
@ref s 83.031(2) (src:1306-1307)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the power, duty or function is conferred on a Minister referred to in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.031(2) the Minister may designate a person to exercise a power, or perform a duty or function` MEANS
    IF     provision's `section` AT LEAST 83.032 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 83.0392
       AND `the power, duty or function is conferred on a Minister referred to in those sections`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any Minister referred to in any of sections 83.032 to 83.0392 may designate a person to exercise a power, or perform a duty or function, conferred on that Minister under those sections"

§ `Section 83.032 -- Authorization`

§§ `83.032(1) and (2) the power to authorize, and what "control" means`

-- (1) The six purposes. "from among the following" names the purposes an authorization may be for.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11 | s 83.032(1) the Public Safety Minister may authorize the activity | s 83.032(1); s 83.032(1)(*
-- src:1308 | Authorization
-- src:1309 | 83.032 (1) On application, the Public Safety Minister may authorize an eligible person to carry out, in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group, a specified activity that would otherwise be prohibited under subsection 83.03(2) — or a specified class of such activities — for any specified purpose from among the following:
-- src:1310 | (a) providing or supporting the provision of health services;
-- src:1311 | (b) providing or supporting the provision of education services;
-- src:1312 | (c) providing or supporting the provision of programs to assist individuals in earning a livelihood;
-- src:1313 | (d) providing or supporting the provision of programs to promote or protect human rights;
-- src:1314 | (e) providing or supporting the provision of services related to immigration, including services related to the resettlement of individuals and the safe passage of individuals from one geographic area to another; and
-- src:1315 | (f) supporting any operations of a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada that are conducted for a purpose other than one set out in any of paragraphs (a) to (e).
@ref s 83.032(1) (src:1308-1315)
DECLARE `s 83.032(1) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.032(1)(a) providing or supporting the provision of health services`
    `s 83.032(1)(b) providing or supporting the provision of education services`
    `s 83.032(1)(c) providing or supporting the provision of programs to assist individuals in earning a livelihood`
    `s 83.032(1)(d) providing or supporting the provision of programs to promote or protect human rights`
    `s 83.032(1)(e) providing or supporting the provision of services related to immigration`
    `s 83.032(1)(f) supporting operations of a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada conducted for another purpose`
    `s 83.032(1) a purpose that is none of those`

DECLARE `s 83.032(1) facts` HAS
    `an application has been made`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity is in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity would otherwise be prohibited under subsection 83.03(2)`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose`                                                                                    IS A `s 83.032(1) purpose`

-- GATE-B (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), listed for a lawyer, fork F-ccc3-11): "On application" gates the whole grant, so with no application the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, "on" counted with "where").
-- GATE-S: the other limits of the grant ("eligible person", "specified", "from among the following") are scope limits with no "only": outside them, NOTHING (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05).
@ref s 83.032(1) (src:1308-1315)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.032(1) facts`
      `the person is eligible, by s 83.032(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(1) the Public Safety Minister may authorize the activity` MEANS
    IF NOT facts's `an application has been made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application, the Public Safety Minister may authorize"
    ELSE IF     `the person is eligible, by s 83.032(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND facts's `the activity is in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group`
            AND facts's `the activity would otherwise be prohibited under subsection 83.03(2)`
            AND NOT (facts's `the purpose` EQUALS `s 83.032(1) a purpose that is none of those`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an eligible person to carry out, in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group, a specified activity"

-- (2) "a terrorist group controls a geographic area if the group exerts sufficient influence over the area such that ... could reasonably be expected to result in".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(2) the terrorist group controls the geographic area | s 83.032(2)
-- src:1316 | Control
-- src:1317 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a terrorist group controls a geographic area if the group exerts sufficient influence over the area such that the carrying out, in the area, of an activity involving property or financial or other related services could reasonably be expected to result in the terrorist group using or benefiting from the property or services, in whole or in part.
@ref s 83.032(2) (src:1316-1317)
GIVEN `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the group exerts sufficient influence over the area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carrying out in the area an activity involving property or financial or other related services could reasonably be expected to result in the terrorist group using or benefiting from the property or services, in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(2) the terrorist group controls the geographic area` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF     `the group exerts sufficient influence over the area`
           AND `carrying out in the area an activity involving property or financial or other related services could reasonably be expected to result in the terrorist group using or benefiting from the property or services, in whole or in part`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a terrorist group controls a geographic area if the group exerts sufficient influence over the area"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a terrorist group controls a geographic area"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group is for s 83.01(1)

§§ `83.032(2.1) to (4) information, a bar, eligibility`

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.032(2.1) the Public Safety Minister must provide information in writing | s 83.032(2.1)
-- src:1318 | Minister’s obligation — information
-- src:1319 | (2.1) The Public Safety Minister must, at the request of an eligible person or an organization, provide to that person or organization information in writing about whether an authorization is required to carry out an activity or a class of activities in a given geographic area.
@ref s 83.032(2.1) (src:1318-1319)
GIVEN `a request has been made by an eligible person or an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it asks whether an authorization is required to carry out an activity or a class of activities in a given geographic area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(2.1) the Public Safety Minister must provide information in writing` MEANS
    IF `a request has been made by an eligible person or an organization` AND `it asks whether an authorization is required to carry out an activity or a class of activities in a given geographic area`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the request of an eligible person or an organization"

-- (3) a bar: the Minister "must not" authorize the grant or contribution.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(3) the Public Safety Minister is barred from authorizing the grant or contribution | s 83.032(3)
-- src:1320 | Limitation
-- src:1321 | (3) The Public Safety Minister must not, under subsection (1), authorize the making by a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada of a grant or contribution that is for the purpose of supporting any operations referred to in paragraph (1)(f).
@ref s 83.032(3) (src:1320-1321)
GIVEN `the activity is the making by a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada of a grant or contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of supporting any operations referred to in paragraph (1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(3) the Public Safety Minister is barred from authorizing the grant or contribution` MEANS
    IF `the activity is the making by a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada of a grant or contribution` AND `it is for the purpose of supporting any operations referred to in paragraph (1)(f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not, under subsection (1), authorize the making by a federal minister or a department or agency of the Government of Canada of a grant or contribution"

-- (4) ENTITLED-group: "is eligible ... if". Read as the status quo reading (a): a failed "if" is the text's no.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-14 | s 83.032(4) the person is eligible to be granted an authorization | s 83.032(4)
-- src:1322 | Eligible persons
-- src:1323 | (4) A person is eligible to be granted an authorization if they are in Canada or are a Canadian outside Canada.
@ref s 83.032(4) (src:1322-1323)
GIVEN `the person is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(4) the person is eligible to be granted an authorization` MEANS
    IF `the person is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- "are a Canadian outside Canada"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is eligible to be granted an authorization if they are in Canada or are a Canadian outside Canada"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a Canadian is for s 83.01(1)

§§ `83.032(5) to (8) referral, conditions of referral, deemed withdrawal, assessment`

-- (5): the referral the application needs depends on which of the six purposes it is in respect of.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(5) the Public Safety Minister may consider the application | s 83.032(5)*
-- src:1324 | Referral
-- src:1325 | (5) The Public Safety Minister may consider an application only if it has been referred to them by
-- src:1326 | (a) the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration, if the application is in respect of only the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e);
-- src:1327 | (b) the Minister of Foreign Affairs, if the application is not in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e); or
-- src:1328 | (c) both of those Ministers, if the application is in respect of two or more purposes set out in subsection (1), at least one of which is the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e).
@ref s 83.032(5) (src:1324-1328)
DECLARE `s 83.032(5) application` HAS
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(a)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(b)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(d)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(f)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been referred by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been referred by the Minister of Foreign Affairs`               IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.032(5) (src:1324-1328)
GIVEN app IS A `s 83.032(5) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(5) the Public Safety Minister may consider the application` MEANS
    IF `s 83.032(5)(a) the application is in respect of only the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)`
    THEN IF app's `it has been referred by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may consider an application only if it has been referred to them by"
    ELSE IF `s 83.032(5)(b) the application is not in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)`
         THEN IF app's `it has been referred by the Minister of Foreign Affairs`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may consider an application only if it has been referred to them by"
         ELSE IF `s 83.032(5)(c) the application is in respect of two or more purposes, at least one of which is the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)`
              THEN IF app's `it has been referred by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration` AND app's `it has been referred by the Minister of Foreign Affairs`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may consider an application only if it has been referred to them by"
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may consider an application only if it has been referred to them by"
    WHERE
        `the number of the other purposes` MEANS
            (IF app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(a)` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(b)` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c)` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(d)` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(f)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        `s 83.032(5)(a) the application is in respect of only the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)` MEANS
            app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)` AND `the number of the other purposes` EQUALS 0
        `s 83.032(5)(b) the application is not in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)` MEANS
            (NOT app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)`) AND `the number of the other purposes` AT LEAST 1
        `s 83.032(5)(c) the application is in respect of two or more purposes, at least one of which is the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)` MEANS
            app's `in respect of the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(e)` AND `the number of the other purposes` AT LEAST 1

-- (6) GATE-A: "may refer an application if they are satisfied that (a) to (e)": a power with an "if" gate: NOTHING when a condition fails.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.032(6) the Minister or Ministers may refer the application | s 83.032(6)*
-- src:1329 | Conditions of referral
-- src:1330 | (6) The Minister of Foreign Affairs, the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or both of those Ministers, as the case may be, may refer an application if they are satisfied that
-- src:1331 | (a) the application meets any requirements set out in the regulations;
-- src:1332 | (b) the geographic area identified in the application is controlled by a terrorist group;
-- src:1333 | (c) the activity proposed in the application is to be carried out for any of the purposes set out in paragraphs (1)(a) to (f);
-- src:1334 | (d) that activity responds to a real and important need in that geographic area; and
-- src:1335 | (e) the applicant is capable of administering funds, and reporting on that administration, in a manner that is transparent and accountable, in circumstances in which a terrorist group may use or benefit from property or financial or other related services.
@ref s 83.032(6) (src:1329-1335)
DECLARE `s 83.032(6) conditions` HAS
    `they are satisfied that the application meets any requirements set out in the regulations`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `they are satisfied that the geographic area identified in the application is controlled by a terrorist group`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `they are satisfied that the activity proposed in the application is to be carried out for any of the purposes set out in paragraphs (1)(a) to (f)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `they are satisfied that the activity responds to a real and important need in that geographic area`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `they are satisfied that the applicant is capable of administering funds, and reporting on that administration, in a manner that is transparent and accountable, in circumstances in which a terrorist group may use or benefit from property or financial or other related services`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)

@ref s 83.032(6) (src:1329-1335)
GIVEN conditions IS A `s 83.032(6) conditions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(6) the Minister or Ministers may refer the application` MEANS
    IF     conditions's `they are satisfied that the application meets any requirements set out in the regulations`
       AND conditions's `they are satisfied that the geographic area identified in the application is controlled by a terrorist group`
       AND conditions's `they are satisfied that the activity proposed in the application is to be carried out for any of the purposes set out in paragraphs (1)(a) to (f)`
       AND conditions's `they are satisfied that the activity responds to a real and important need in that geographic area`
       AND conditions's `they are satisfied that the applicant is capable of administering funds, and reporting on that administration, in a manner that is transparent and accountable, in circumstances in which a terrorist group may use or benefit from property or financial or other related services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may refer an application if they are satisfied that"

-- (7) GATE-A: "An application may be deemed to be withdrawn ... if the applicant has, within 60 days after the day on which the request is made, failed to comply".
-- The 60 days run from the day after the request is made; the 60th day is `request day + 60`. A failure is established once that day has passed without the information.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.032(7) the application may be deemed to be withdrawn | s 83.032(7)
-- src:1336 | Deemed withdrawal
-- src:1337 | (7) An application may be deemed to be withdrawn by the Minister or Ministers who may refer it if the applicant has, within 60 days after the day on which the request is made, failed to comply with a request to provide information that ought to have been included in the application.
@ref s 83.032(7) (src:1336-1337)
GIVEN `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant provided the information, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(7) the application may be deemed to be withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the question is asked` AT LEAST ((`the day on which the request is made` PLUS 60) PLUS 1)
    THEN CONSIDER `the day on which the applicant provided the information, if it did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST provided THEN
             IF provided AT MOST (`the day on which the request is made` PLUS 60)
             THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be deemed to be withdrawn by the Minister or Ministers who may refer it if the applicant has"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be deemed to be withdrawn by the Minister or Ministers who may refer it if the applicant has"

-- (8) a duty of the referring Minister, met or not (a bare "must": fork F-ccc3-6, decided case by case).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.032(8) the referral sets out the assessment | s 83.032(8)
-- src:1338 | Assessment
-- src:1339 | (8) The Minister who refers an application must, as part of the referral, set out their assessment of how the application meets the conditions set out in paragraphs (6)(a) to (e).
@ref s 83.032(8) (src:1338-1339)
GIVEN `the referral sets out their assessment of how the application meets each of the conditions in paragraphs (6)(a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(8) the referral sets out the assessment` MEANS
    IF `the referral sets out their assessment of how the application meets each of the conditions in paragraphs (6)(a) to (e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, as part of the referral, set out their assessment"

§§ `83.032(9) to (12) the grant, the security review, further information, terms and conditions`

-- (9) GATE-A: "may grant the authorization ... if they are satisfied that (a) ...; and (b) ...".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.032(9) the Public Safety Minister may grant the authorization | s 83.032(9)*
-- src:1340 | Conditions for grant
-- src:1341 | (9) The Public Safety Minister may grant the authorization under subsection (1) if they are satisfied that
-- src:1342 | (a) there is no practical way to carry out the activity proposed in the application without creating a risk that, in whole or in part, a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or financial or related services at issue; and
-- src:1343 | (b) the benefits of carrying out of that activity outweigh that risk, taking into account
-- src:1344 | (i) the referral of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or both of those Ministers, as the case may be,
-- src:1345 | (ii) the security review conducted by the Public Safety Minister under subsection (10),
-- src:1346 | (iii) any mitigation measures to minimize that risk, and any other terms and conditions, that may be included in the authorization, and
-- src:1347 | (iv) any other factor that the Public Safety Minister considers appropriate in the circumstances.
@ref s 83.032(9) (src:1340-1347)
DECLARE `s 83.032(9) conditions` HAS
    `they are satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity proposed in the application without creating a risk that, in whole or in part, a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or financial or related services at issue`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `they are satisfied that the benefits of carrying out of that activity outweigh that risk`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `they took into account the referral`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
    `they took into account the security review conducted under subsection (10)`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
    `they took into account any mitigation measures to minimize that risk, and any other terms and conditions, that may be included in the authorization`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)

@ref s 83.032(9) (src:1340-1347)
GIVEN conditions IS A `s 83.032(9) conditions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(9) the Public Safety Minister may grant the authorization` MEANS
    IF     conditions's `they are satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity proposed in the application without creating a risk that, in whole or in part, a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or financial or related services at issue`
       AND conditions's `they are satisfied that the benefits of carrying out of that activity outweigh that risk`
       AND conditions's `they took into account the referral`
       AND conditions's `they took into account the security review conducted under subsection (10)`
       AND conditions's `they took into account any mitigation measures to minimize that risk, and any other terms and conditions, that may be included in the authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may grant the authorization under subsection (1) if they are satisfied that"

-- (10) "must assess the impact ... and in doing so may consider, among other factors, (a) to (c)": the list is open, so a factor outside it is not covered.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(10) the factor may be considered in the security review | s 83.032(10)*
-- src:1348 | Security review
-- src:1349 | (10) In conducting a security review, the Public Safety Minister must assess the impact of granting the authorization on the financing of terrorism, and in doing so may consider, among other factors,
-- src:1350 | (a) whether the applicant or any person who is to be involved in carrying out the activity proposed in the application has any links to a terrorist group;
-- src:1351 | (b) the likelihood that the applicant or any person who is to be involved in carrying out that activity will be acting for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group in carrying out the activity; and
-- src:1352 | (c) whether the applicant or any person who is to be involved in carrying out that activity is being or has been investigated for having committed a terrorism offence or has ever been charged with a terrorism offence.
@ref s 83.032(10) (src:1348-1352)
DECLARE `s 83.032(10) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.032(10)(a) whether the applicant or any person to be involved has any links to a terrorist group`
    `s 83.032(10)(b) the likelihood that the applicant or any person to be involved will be acting for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group`
    `s 83.032(10)(c) whether the applicant or any person to be involved is being or has been investigated for, or has ever been charged with, a terrorism offence`
    `s 83.032(10) another factor`

@ref s 83.032(10) (src:1348-1352)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 83.032(10) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(10) the factor may be considered in the security review` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 83.032(10)(a) whether the applicant or any person to be involved has any links to a terrorist group` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.032(10)(b) the likelihood that the applicant or any person to be involved will be acting for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.032(10)(c) whether the applicant or any person to be involved is being or has been investigated for, or has ever been charged with, a terrorism offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.032(10) another factor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may consider, among other factors"

@ref s 83.032(10) (src:1348-1349)
GIVEN `the review assessed the impact of granting the authorization on the financing of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(10) the security review assesses the impact on the financing of terrorism` MEANS
    IF `the review assessed the impact of granting the authorization on the financing of terrorism`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must assess the impact of granting the authorization on the financing of terrorism"

-- (11) The first sentence is a power to request, the second a GATE-A power to deem the application withdrawn.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.032(11) the Public Safety Minister may request additional information; s 83.032(11) the Public Safety Minister may deem the application to be withdrawn | s 83.032(11)
-- src:1353 | Additional information
-- src:1354 | (11) The Public Safety Minister may request that the applicant provide any additional information in respect of the application in the form and manner, and within the period, that are specified by that Minister. If the applicant fails, without reasonable excuse, to provide the information within the specified period, that Minister may deem the application to be withdrawn.
@ref s 83.032(11) (src:1353-1354)
GIVEN `the information is additional information in respect of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(11) the Public Safety Minister may request additional information` MEANS
    IF `the information is additional information in respect of the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may request that the applicant provide any additional information in respect of the application"

@ref s 83.032(11) (src:1353-1354)
GIVEN `the applicant failed to provide the information within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(11) the Public Safety Minister may deem the application to be withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the applicant failed to provide the information within the specified period` AND `without reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the applicant fails, without reasonable excuse, to provide the information within the specified period, that Minister may deem the application to be withdrawn"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(12) the Public Safety Minister may make the authorization subject to the terms and conditions | s 83.032(12)
-- src:1355 | Terms and conditions
-- src:1356 | (12) The Public Safety Minister may make the authorization subject to any terms and conditions that, in their opinion, are required.
@ref s 83.032(12) (src:1355-1356)
GIVEN `in the Minister’s opinion the terms and conditions are required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(12) the Public Safety Minister may make the authorization subject to the terms and conditions` MEANS
    IF `in the Minister’s opinion the terms and conditions are required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any terms and conditions that, in their opinion, are required"

§§ `83.032(13) to (16) other persons involved, the period of validity, the Security Council, the Statutory Instruments Act`

-- (13) The authorization reaches the person it is granted to, and any other person involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out the specified activity in accordance with it.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(13) the authorization applies to the person | s 83.032(13)
-- src:1357 | Third party involvement
-- src:1358 | (13) An authorization applies not only to the person to whom it is granted but also to any other person involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization.
@ref s 83.032(13) (src:1357-1358)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the authorization is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(13) the authorization applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom the authorization is granted` OR `the person is involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies not only to the person to whom it is granted but also to any other person involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization"

-- (14) "valid for the period of not more than five years that is specified in the authorization". `Length of time` keeps the text's units (core).
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(14) the specified period is not more than five years; s 83.032(14) the authorization is valid on the day | s 83.032(14)
-- src:1359 | Period of validity
-- src:1360 | (14) An authorization is valid for the period of not more than five years that is specified in the authorization.
@ref s 83.032(14) (src:1359-1360)
GIVEN period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(14) the specified period is not more than five years` MEANS
    IF (period's years TIMES 12) PLUS period's months LESS THAN 60 OR ((period's years TIMES 12) PLUS period's months EQUALS 60 AND period's days EQUALS 0)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid for the period of not more than five years"

@ref s 83.032(14) (src:1359-1360)
GIVEN `the day on which the authorization takes effect` IS A DATE
      period IS A `Length of time`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(14) the authorization is valid on the day` MEANS
    IF `s 83.032(14) the specified period is not more than five years` period EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day on which the authorization takes effect` AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the last day of validity`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorization is valid for the period of not more than five years that is specified in the authorization"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid for the period of not more than five years"
    WHERE
        `the last day of validity` MEANS (`add months` `the day on which the authorization takes effect` ((period's years TIMES 12) PLUS period's months)) PLUS (period's days MINUS 1)

-- (15) "may authorize ... only if the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that (a), (b) or (c)": a closed gate, so JUST FALSE when none is confirmed.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11 | s 83.032(15) the Public Safety Minister may authorize the activity benefiting a listed entity under a Security Council sanctions regime | s 83.032(15)*
-- src:1361 | Decisions of the United Nations Security Council
-- src:1362 | (15) In the case of an activity proposed in an application in the course of which property or financial or other related services will be used by or will benefit a listed entity that is subject to a sanctions regime established by the Security Council of the United Nations, the Public Safety Minister may authorize the carrying out of that activity only if the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that
-- src:1363 | (a) the Security Council did not intend that the activity be prohibited;
-- src:1364 | (b) the Security Council or a Committee established by the Security Council has approved the activity in advance; or
-- src:1365 | (c) in the opinion of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, there is no obstacle in international law to granting the authorization.
@ref s 83.032(15) (src:1361-1365)
GIVEN `the activity is one in the course of which property or financial or other related services will be used by or will benefit a listed entity that is subject to a sanctions regime established by the Security Council of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that the Security Council did not intend that the activity be prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that the Security Council or a Committee established by the Security Council has approved the activity in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that in the Minister’s opinion there is no obstacle in international law to granting the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(15) the Public Safety Minister may authorize the activity benefiting a listed entity under a Security Council sanctions regime` MEANS
    IF NOT `the activity is one in the course of which property or financial or other related services will be used by or will benefit a listed entity that is subject to a sanctions regime established by the Security Council of the United Nations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of an activity proposed in an application in the course of which property or financial or other related services will be used by or will benefit a listed entity that is subject to a sanctions regime established by the Security Council of the United Nations"
    ELSE IF     `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that the Security Council did not intend that the activity be prohibited`
             OR `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that the Security Council or a Committee established by the Security Council has approved the activity in advance`
             OR `the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that in the Minister’s opinion there is no obstacle in international law to granting the authorization`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may authorize the carrying out of that activity only if the Minister of Foreign Affairs confirms that"

-- (16) a flat negative about authorizations only.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.032(16) the Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to the instrument | s 83.032(16)
-- src:1366 | Statutory Instruments Act
-- src:1367 | (16) The Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to an authorization.
@ref s 83.032(16) (src:1366-1367)
GIVEN `the instrument is an authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.032(16) the Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is an authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to an authorization"

§ `Section 83.033 -- Notice of refusal; waiting period; a new application`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.033(1) the notice of refusal is given within a reasonable time | s 83.033(1)
-- src:1368 | Notice of refusal
-- src:1369 | 83.033 (1) The Public Safety Minister, the Minister of Foreign Affairs or the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration, as the case may be, must give notice of a decision to refuse an application made under section 83.032 to the applicant within a reasonable time.
@ref s 83.033(1) (src:1368-1369)
GIVEN `notice of the decision to refuse the application has been given to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was given within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.033(1) the notice of refusal is given within a reasonable time` MEANS
    IF `notice of the decision to refuse the application has been given to the applicant` AND `it was given within a reasonable time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give notice of a decision to refuse an application made under section 83.032 to the applicant within a reasonable time"

-- (2) a bar "until the end of the 30th day after the day on which the notice is given": JUST TRUE (barred) through that day, JUST FALSE after it (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05).
-- "unless the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances": once met, the bar is lifted (fork F-ccc3-5).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-5 | s 83.033(2) the applicant is barred from making a new application | s 83.033(2)
-- src:1370 | Waiting period — new application
-- src:1371 | (2) An applicant whose application is refused is not permitted to make a new application in respect of the same activity until the end of the 30th day after the day on which the notice is given, unless the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances.
@ref s 83.033(2) (src:1370-1371)
GIVEN `the new application is in respect of the same activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the new application is made` IS A DATE
      `the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.033(2) the applicant is barred from making a new application` MEANS
    IF NOT `the new application is in respect of the same activity`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not permitted to make a new application in respect of the same activity"
    ELSE IF `the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances"
         ELSE IF `the day on which the new application is made` AT MOST (`the day on which the notice is given` PLUS 30)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the end of the 30th day after the day on which the notice is given"

-- (3) GATE-A: "If the Public Safety Minister gave the notice and is satisfied as described in subsection (2), that Minister may consider the new application without it having been referred".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.033(3) the Public Safety Minister may consider the new application without a referral | s 83.033(3)
-- src:1372 | Consideration of new application without referral
-- src:1373 | (3) If the Public Safety Minister gave the notice and is satisfied as described in subsection (2), that Minister may consider the new application without it having been referred under subsection 83.032(5). In that case, that Minister may take into account the referral of the previous application for the purposes of subparagraph 83.032(9)(b)(i).
@ref s 83.033(3) (src:1372-1373)
GIVEN `the Public Safety Minister gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that Minister is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.033(3) the Public Safety Minister may consider the new application without a referral` MEANS
    IF `the Public Safety Minister gave the notice` AND `that Minister is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Public Safety Minister gave the notice and is satisfied as described in subsection (2), that Minister may consider the new application without it having been referred"

§ `Sections 83.034 to 83.037 -- Additional reviews, renewal, amendment, suspension and revocation`

-- 83.034 GATE-B: "At any time during the period of validity" is a period gate: outside it, JUST FALSE (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05); a person the authorization does not apply to is outside the grant (NOTHING).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11 | s 83.034 the Public Safety Minister may conduct an additional security review; s 83.034 the request for additional information may be made | s 83.034
-- src:1374 | Additional security reviews
-- src:1375 | 83.034 At any time during the period of validity of an authorization granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035, the Public Safety Minister may conduct additional security reviews under subsection 83.032(10) in respect of any person to whom the authorization applies. For the purpose of those reviews, that Minister may request that the person to whom the authorization is granted provide any additional information in the form and manner, and within the period, that are specified by that Minister, but the request must relate only to the authorization or its renewal.
@ref s 83.034 (src:1374-1375)
GIVEN `the day on which the review is to be conducted` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period of validity` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period of validity` IS A DATE
      `the authorization applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.034 the Public Safety Minister may conduct an additional security review` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day on which the review is to be conducted` AT LEAST `the first day of the period of validity` AND `the day on which the review is to be conducted` AT MOST `the last day of the period of validity`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At any time during the period of validity of an authorization granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035"
    ELSE IF `the authorization applies to the person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any person to whom the authorization applies"

@ref s 83.034 (src:1374-1375)
GIVEN `the request relates only to the authorization or its renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.034 the request for additional information may be made` MEANS
    IF `the request relates only to the authorization or its renewal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but the request must relate only to the authorization or its renewal"

-- 83.035(1) GATE-B: "on application ... made within any period set out in the regulations and before the authorization expires"; "for successive periods of not more than five years each".
-- The last day of validity is the last day on which the authorization is valid: an application made on or before it is "before the authorization expires" (fork F-ccc3-7).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-7,F-ccc3-11 | s 83.035(1) the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization | s 83.035(1)
-- src:1376 | Renewal of authorization
-- src:1377 | 83.035 (1) The Public Safety Minister may renew an authorization granted under section 83.032 for successive periods of not more than five years each on application, for each renewal, made within any period set out in the regulations and before the authorization expires.
@ref s 83.035(1) (src:1376-1377)
GIVEN `an application has been made for the renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was made within any period set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the authorization is valid` IS A DATE
      `the period for which renewal is sought` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.035(1) the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application has been made for the renewal`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application, for each renewal"
    ELSE IF NOT `the application was made within any period set out in the regulations`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made within any period set out in the regulations and before the authorization expires"
         ELSE IF `the day on which the application was made` GREATER THAN `the last day on which the authorization is valid`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made within any period set out in the regulations and before the authorization expires"
              ELSE IF `s 83.032(14) the specified period is not more than five years` `the period for which renewal is sought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for successive periods of not more than five years each"

-- 83.035(2) GATE-A: "Despite subsection (1), if an application for renewal is made after the authorization expires, the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization if, in that Minister's opinion, there are exceptional circumstances".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-7,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.035(2) the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization on a late application | s 83.035(2)
-- src:1378 | Exception
-- src:1379 | (2) Despite subsection (1), if an application for renewal is made after the authorization expires, the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization if, in that Minister’s opinion, there are exceptional circumstances that justify why the application for renewal was not made before it expired.
@ref s 83.035(2) (src:1378-1379)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the authorization is valid` IS A DATE
      `in that Minister’s opinion there are exceptional circumstances that justify why the application for renewal was not made before it expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.035(2) the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization on a late application` MEANS
    IF     `the day on which the application was made` GREATER THAN `the last day on which the authorization is valid`
       AND `in that Minister’s opinion there are exceptional circumstances that justify why the application for renewal was not made before it expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an application for renewal is made after the authorization expires, the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization if, in that Minister’s opinion, there are exceptional circumstances"

-- 83.036(1): the power to amend, "including any terms and conditions included in it".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.036(1) the Public Safety Minister may amend the authorization | s 83.036(1)
-- src:1380 | Amendment to authorization
-- src:1381 | 83.036 (1) The Public Safety Minister may amend an authorization granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035, including any terms and conditions included in it.
@ref s 83.036(1) (src:1380-1381)
GIVEN `the authorization was granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.036(1) the Public Safety Minister may amend the authorization` MEANS
    IF `the authorization was granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may amend an authorization granted under section 83.032 or renewed under section 83.035"

-- (2) a bar: "is not permitted to amend ... if the amendment would be so significant as to change the essential nature of the authorization, including if the amendment would replace a purpose ... or add another such purpose".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-21 | s 83.036(2) the Public Safety Minister is not permitted to make the amendment | s 83.036(2)
-- src:1382 | Exception
-- src:1383 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Public Safety Minister is not permitted to amend an authorization if the amendment would be so significant as to change the essential nature of the authorization, including if the amendment would replace a purpose set out in subsection 83.032(1) and specified in the authorization or add another such purpose.
@ref s 83.036(2) (src:1382-1383)
GIVEN `the amendment would be so significant as to change the essential nature of the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment would replace a purpose set out in subsection 83.032(1) and specified in the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment would add another such purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.036(2) the Public Safety Minister is not permitted to make the amendment` MEANS
    IF     `the amendment would be so significant as to change the essential nature of the authorization`
        OR `the amendment would replace a purpose set out in subsection 83.032(1) and specified in the authorization`
        OR `the amendment would add another such purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not permitted to amend an authorization if the amendment would be so significant as to change the essential nature of the authorization"

-- (3) a duty of the holder, which arises only for information "specified by that Minister in support of the amendment".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.036(3) the person to whom the authorization is granted must provide the information | s 83.036(3)
-- src:1384 | Supporting information
-- src:1385 | (3) The person to whom the authorization is granted must provide to the Public Safety Minister any information specified by that Minister in support of the amendment.
@ref s 83.036(3) (src:1384-1385)
GIVEN `the Public Safety Minister specified the information in support of the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.036(3) the person to whom the authorization is granted must provide the information` MEANS
    IF `the Public Safety Minister specified the information in support of the amendment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information specified by that Minister in support of the amendment"

-- 83.037 GATE-A: "may ... suspend or revoke it or restrict its scope if (a), (b) or (c)".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.037 the Public Safety Minister may suspend or revoke the authorization or restrict its scope | s 83.037*
-- src:1386 | Authorization — suspension and revocation
-- src:1387 | 83.037 The Public Safety Minister may, at any time after granting an authorization under section 83.032, suspend or revoke it or restrict its scope if
-- src:1388 | (a) a person to whom the authorization applies fails to comply with the authorization, including any terms and conditions included in it;
-- src:1389 | (b) the person to whom the authorization is granted fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with any reporting requirements or to provide any information requested under section 83.034; or
-- src:1390 | (c) the Public Safety Minister is no longer satisfied that the condition set out in paragraph 83.032(9)(b) is met.
@ref s 83.037 (src:1386-1390)
GIVEN `the authorization was granted under section 83.032` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person to whom the authorization applies fails to comply with the authorization, including any terms and conditions included in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the authorization is granted fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with any reporting requirements or to provide any information requested under section 83.034` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Public Safety Minister is no longer satisfied that the condition set out in paragraph 83.032(9)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.037 the Public Safety Minister may suspend or revoke the authorization or restrict its scope` MEANS
    IF     `the authorization was granted under section 83.032`
       AND (    `a person to whom the authorization applies fails to comply with the authorization, including any terms and conditions included in it`
             OR `the person to whom the authorization is granted fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with any reporting requirements or to provide any information requested under section 83.034`
             OR `the Public Safety Minister is no longer satisfied that the condition set out in paragraph 83.032(9)(b) is met`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "suspend or revoke it or restrict its scope if"

§ `Sections 83.038 and 83.039 -- Assistance to the Minister; judicial review`

-- 83.038(1): the entities that may assist. The list is a grant without "only", so an entity not named and not prescribed is not covered.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.038(1) the entity may assist the Public Safety Minister | s 83.038(1)*
-- src:1391 | Assistance to Public Safety Minister
-- src:1392 | 83.038 (1) The following entities may assist the Public Safety Minister in the administration and enforcement of sections 83.031 to 83.0392, including by collecting information from and disclosing information to that Minister and each other:
-- src:1393 | (a) the Canadian Security Intelligence Service;
-- src:1394 | (b) the Royal Canadian Mounted Police;
-- src:1395 | (c) the Communications Security Establishment;
-- src:1396 | (d) the Department of National Defence;
-- src:1397 | (e) the Canadian Armed Forces;
-- src:1398 | (f) the Department of Foreign Affairs, Trade and Development;
-- src:1399 | (g) the Canada Revenue Agency;
-- src:1400 | (h) the Canada Border Services Agency;
-- src:1401 | (i) the Department of Citizenship and Immigration; and
-- src:1402 | (j) any other entity prescribed by regulation.
@ref s 83.038(1) (src:1391-1402)
DECLARE `s 83.038(1) entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.038(1)(a) the Canadian Security Intelligence Service`
    `s 83.038(1)(b) the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
    `s 83.038(1)(c) the Communications Security Establishment`
    `s 83.038(1)(d) the Department of National Defence`
    `s 83.038(1)(e) the Canadian Armed Forces`
    `s 83.038(1)(f) the Department of Foreign Affairs, Trade and Development`
    `s 83.038(1)(g) the Canada Revenue Agency`
    `s 83.038(1)(h) the Canada Border Services Agency`
    `s 83.038(1)(i) the Department of Citizenship and Immigration`
    `s 83.038(1)(j) another entity prescribed by regulation`
    `s 83.038(1) an entity that is neither named in paragraphs (a) to (i) nor prescribed by regulation`

@ref s 83.038(1) (src:1391-1402)
GIVEN entity IS A `s 83.038(1) entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.038(1) the entity may assist the Public Safety Minister` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `s 83.038(1) an entity that is neither named in paragraphs (a) to (i) nor prescribed by regulation` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following entities may assist the Public Safety Minister"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

