§ `Sections 83.0391 and 83.0392 -- Regulations; annual report; review`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.0392(1) the last day for laying the report; s 83.0392(1) the report is laid within the time | s 83.0392(1)
-- src:1432 | Annual report
-- src:1433 | 83.0392 (1) The Public Safety Minister must prepare and cause to be laid before each House of Parliament, within 90 days after the first day of January of every year, a report on the operation of sections 83.031 to 83.0391 for the previous calendar year.
@ref s 83.0392(1) (src:1432-1433)
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 83.0392(1) the last day for laying the report` MEANS (Date 1 1 `the calendar year`) PLUS 90

@ref s 83.0392(1) (src:1432-1433)
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the report is laid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.0392(1) the report is laid within the time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the report is laid` LESS THAN (Date 1 1 `the calendar year`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether a report laid before the first day of January is "within 90 days after" it
    ELSE IF `the day on which the report is laid` AT MOST `s 83.0392(1) the last day for laying the report` `the calendar year`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after the first day of January of every year"

